  "notes": ["The two exact melee hits and corresponding whiffs leave the normal Sasuke receiver in guest memory. Only its clock is visited.","Movement speed, heading gap, lane mask and reference frame are declared. The original wait is installed by the VM from its indexed command.","The wait and clip are source probe commands, not inferred choices of this receiver's controller.","The planar helper reads the primary rate. Heading, the finite wait, and the relative-frame clip request read the secondary rate.","The explicit frame bypasses the relative rate calculation. Both clip probes stop at the original request before sampling any pose.","Direct call counts are static, not qualified call schedules. No live movement sweep, actor frame loop, pose playback or native gameplay runs."],
